      "created_at": "2013-05-15T15:57:05.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>We ran into an odd sort of situation the other night.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Playing against La Capitain, she had grabbed various cards, stacked them under herself and flipped over. Tempest was his promo version and we were curious that with the way his ability is worded, you could potentially interpret that as letting him destroy one of \"his\" cards that was under her. Do they cease to be his cards at that point or can he knock out from under her and draw 3 at the same time?</p>",
