      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/f0a364/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2013-05-15T17:15:34.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Foote\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/48/1877_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Foote:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I would say that you cannont \"Sac\" a card under her. She stole it. It is no longer in your possesion to sacrifice. I would be surprised if there was a ruling to the contrary here.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>You actually \"Destroy\" the card, which is the same thing she does when the damage trigger goes off.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Here's Tempest's power wording</p>\n<p>Power: Destroy 1 of your cards. If you do, draw 3 cards.</p>",
