      "username": "brytehfryguy",
      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/b/f0a364/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2013-05-15T17:46:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Cosmonaut Zero\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n Cosmonaut Zero:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>The only potential hitch is to define \"your.\" Does it mean \"in front of you in your play area,\" or does it mean, \"a card belonging to your deck?\"I think there's a fair argument to be made either way.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Well, it would have to be more specific than \"in front of you in your play area\" as their are villian cards that end up there and cards of yours that end up in the villian play area.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>I suppose that Tempest could potentially not be allowed to use Sacrifice on Vicious Cyclone.</p>",
